1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,414
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,078 --> 00:00:15,507
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,557 --> 00:00:18,379
The Little Lion and the Brave Mouse!

7
00:00:22,998 --> 00:00:28,601
Once upon a time, on a warm golden
savanna, there was a little lion named

8
00:00:28,651 --> 00:00:29,851
Rafi.

9
00:00:30,331 --> 00:00:36,072
Rafi still had a short, soft mane, and
he loved to play hunter among the tall

10
00:00:36,122 --> 00:00:37,322
grasses.

11
00:00:37,887 --> 00:00:43,420
That sunny morning, he ran, jumped,
and rolled on the soft ground,

12
00:00:43,470 --> 00:00:44,870
full of energy.

13
00:00:47,844 --> 00:00:52,924
Suddenly, right under his paw, a tiny
little mouse jumped with a start.

14
00:00:53,566 --> 00:00:55,566
Please, please, don't hurt me!

15
00:00:55,616 --> 00:01:00,336
the little mouse begged in a
very thin, slightly shaky voice.

16
00:01:01,421 --> 00:01:06,496
Little lion Rafi slowly lifted his paw
and looked at the tiny creature with

17
00:01:06,546 --> 00:01:07,821
curiosity.

18
00:01:08,507 --> 00:01:11,029
Who are you, such a tiny little creature?

19
00:01:11,079 --> 00:01:14,160
Rafi asked, tilting his golden head.

20
00:01:14,795 --> 00:01:19,311
I'm Mel, a little mouse of the savanna,
and I was only looking for some seeds

21
00:01:19,361 --> 00:01:20,473
for my lunch,

22
00:01:20,523 --> 00:01:24,700
Mel answered, her little
heart still beating fast.

23
00:01:25,330 --> 00:01:29,772
Then Popcorn the little owl
landed on a dry branch nearby,

24
00:01:29,872 --> 00:01:31,716
straightening her red bow.

25
00:01:32,318 --> 00:01:33,694
Hoo, hoo!

26
00:01:33,798 --> 00:01:35,839
What an interesting meeting!

27
00:01:35,995 --> 00:01:40,260
Sometimes we find friends in
the most unexpected places,

28
00:01:40,310 --> 00:01:44,126
Popcorn said with a clever little smile.

29
00:01:45,223 --> 00:01:50,776
Rafi thought for a moment, and his
little heart grew soft like his new mane.

30
00:01:51,423 --> 00:01:54,061
You are so tiny I almost didn't see you.

31
00:01:54,275 --> 00:01:55,768
You may go in peace, Mel,

32
00:01:55,818 --> 00:01:59,717
Rafi said, opening his paw very gently.

33
00:02:00,385 --> 00:02:04,743
Mel gave a happy little hop and
made a very serious little bow.

34
00:02:05,403 --> 00:02:08,461
Thank you so much, Mister Little Lion!

35
00:02:08,678 --> 00:02:11,851
Someday, who knows, I might
be able to help you too,

36
00:02:11,901 --> 00:02:15,453
Mel promised in a firm, brave voice.

37
00:02:16,095 --> 00:02:17,357
A little mouse help me?

38
00:02:17,569 --> 00:02:18,984
What a funny little idea!

39
00:02:19,034 --> 00:02:22,490
Rafi laughed, shaking
his mane in the breeze.

40
00:02:22,656 --> 00:02:27,273
Mel disappeared into the grass, and
Rafi went back to playing under the warm

41
00:02:27,323 --> 00:02:28,751
savanna sun.

42
00:02:29,856 --> 00:02:34,589
A few days later, when the sun was
saying goodbye on the golden horizon,

43
00:02:34,787 --> 00:02:38,339
Rafi went out to explore a new path.

44
00:02:40,128 --> 00:02:45,578
Suddenly, a very strong net fell from
above and covered the little lion

45
00:02:45,628 --> 00:02:46,828
completely.

46
00:02:47,397 --> 00:02:53,069
Rafi pulled, pushed, and turned every
which way, but the net only grew

47
00:02:53,119 --> 00:02:54,319
tighter.

48
00:02:54,813 --> 00:02:57,638
Help, I'm trapped and I
can't get out by myself!

49
00:02:57,688 --> 00:03:02,601
Rafi roared, his voice
full of fear and sadness.

50
00:03:03,236 --> 00:03:08,575
Nobody from the savanna appeared at
that moment, and the sky grew orange and

51
00:03:08,625 --> 00:03:09,825
quiet.

52
00:03:10,862 --> 00:03:16,687
Far away, little Mel heard that call
and raised her tiny ears right away.

53
00:03:17,336 --> 00:03:20,012
That roar sounds like Rafi's voice!

54
00:03:20,236 --> 00:03:22,557
I need to run and see what happened,

55
00:03:22,607 --> 00:03:26,063
Mel said, already racing
through the grass.

56
00:03:28,957 --> 00:03:34,093
Popcorn flew low beside the little
mouse, flapping her wings carefully.

57
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:36,077
Hoo, hoo!

58
00:03:36,163 --> 00:03:38,763
Let's go together, little one.

59
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:43,543
Sometimes the most important help
comes from the one we least expect,

60
00:03:43,593 --> 00:03:47,354
Popcorn said, cheering Mel along the way.

61
00:03:48,002 --> 00:03:51,855
They reached the clearing and
saw Rafi all wrapped in the net,

62
00:03:51,905 --> 00:03:54,208
his eyes shining with worry.

63
00:03:55,329 --> 00:03:57,506
Don't be afraid, Rafi!

64
00:03:57,693 --> 00:04:02,070
I will gnaw these ropes, one
by one, until you are free,

65
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:05,464
Mel announced in a
determined little voice.

66
00:04:08,431 --> 00:04:13,061
The little mouse began to gnaw
the thinnest rope, very softly,

67
00:04:13,111 --> 00:04:15,303
with great patience and care.

68
00:04:15,928 --> 00:04:22,044
Rafi stayed quiet, breathing deeply,
and for the first time he felt a warm

69
00:04:22,094 --> 00:04:23,814
hope in his chest.

70
00:04:24,441 --> 00:04:28,272
You are so tiny, Mel, but
your heart is enormous,

71
00:04:28,322 --> 00:04:31,097
Rafi murmured in a calmer voice.

72
00:04:31,748 --> 00:04:36,857
Popcorn watched from a branch, not
interrupting her friend's careful work.

73
00:04:40,981 --> 00:04:45,214
After many brave little
bites, the last rope opened,

74
00:04:45,314 --> 00:04:48,853
and the net fell onto
the soft savanna ground.

75
00:04:49,489 --> 00:04:55,176
Rafi leapt out and stretched every paw,
free again under the golden evening

76
00:04:55,226 --> 00:04:56,426
light.

77
00:04:56,664 --> 00:04:58,764
Dear Mel, you really saved me!

78
00:04:58,987 --> 00:05:01,243
I was wrong when I
laughed at your promise,

79
00:05:01,293 --> 00:05:05,068
Rafi said, lowering
his head with kindness.

80
00:05:05,707 --> 00:05:10,107
Mel cleaned her little whiskers
and opened a smile from ear to ear.

81
00:05:10,738 --> 00:05:14,025
I only returned the kindness
you showed me that day,

82
00:05:14,075 --> 00:05:17,322
Mel answered, proud and happy.

83
00:05:17,969 --> 00:05:23,022
The two little friends snuggled close
together on the soft savanna grass.

84
00:05:23,373 --> 00:05:27,032
The little lion and the tiny
mouse were different in size,

85
00:05:27,082 --> 00:05:30,579
but very equal in a
heart full of kindness.

86
00:05:31,658 --> 00:05:36,774
When night arrived on the savanna, the
little stars lit up one by one in the

87
00:05:36,824 --> 00:05:38,044
dark sky.

88
00:05:38,723 --> 00:05:43,984
Popcorn straightened her red bow and
landed right beside the two friends.

89
00:05:44,572 --> 00:05:45,949
Hoo, hoo!

90
00:05:46,055 --> 00:05:49,593
What a beautiful story of
courage and friendship!

91
00:05:49,939 --> 00:05:55,376
Nobody is too small to help, and
kindness always finds its way back,

92
00:05:55,426 --> 00:05:58,465
Popcorn said in a sweet little voice.

93
00:05:59,119 --> 00:06:03,444
Rafi and Mel looked at each other and
smiled, already knowing they would be

94
00:06:03,494 --> 00:06:04,922
friends forever.

95
00:06:05,549 --> 00:06:11,685
And out on the quiet savanna, the
crickets began to sing a very gentle song.

96
00:06:18,963 --> 00:06:20,163
The End.

97
00:06:21,871 --> 00:06:22,583
Hoo...

98
00:06:22,633 --> 00:06:23,657
Psst!

99
00:06:23,707 --> 00:06:25,279
Are you still awake?

100
00:06:25,433 --> 00:06:27,487
Did you like tonight's story?

101
00:06:27,620 --> 00:06:31,802
Rafi and Mel showed us that
nobody is too small to help,

102
00:06:31,852 --> 00:06:35,117
and that kindness always
finds its way back.

103
00:06:35,411 --> 00:06:39,717
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

104
00:06:40,013 --> 00:06:44,911
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

105
00:06:44,961 --> 00:06:47,367
for more stories at bedtime.

106
00:06:47,670 --> 00:06:48,870
Hoo...

